{"id":"29ec509b-e864-4df2-bb68-384e3d587094","url":"http://127.0.0.1:4199/setup/OWzJfFkDkNiEp9vF-lL0mVacoPTV8-1k","prompt":"Install sloppa for PR screenshots, recordings and dev server previews in your app.\n\n1. Find your app's supported MCP configuration method.\n   Use user scope for all projects. Name the server sloppa, replacing any named sloppa or sloppa-artifacts.\n   Configure streamable HTTP at http://127.0.0.1:4199/mcp with \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\".\n\n2. Keep tool output and chat free of the token, including configuration readbacks.\n   With shell tracing disabled, run these three steps in one shell command, chained with &&:\n   - capture the token:\n     TOKEN=$(curl -fsS 'http://127.0.0.1:4199/setup/OWzJfFkDkNiEp9vF-lL0mVacoPTV8-1k' --data-urlencode \"agent=<app> on $(hostname)\")\n   - persist it for your app\n   - check it:\n     curl -fsS 'http://127.0.0.1:4199/api/session' -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\n   Replace <app> with only your app's name, such as Codex or Claude Code.\n   For Codex, use --bearer-token-env-var and save that variable in $CODEX_HOME/.env (default ~/.codex/.env) for startup.\n\nSetup is complete when the user-scope configuration is saved and the session check returns {\"username\":...}.\nA 410 means the link expired or was revoked; ask me for a new one.\n\nThen tell me how to reload your MCP servers, and ask whether to revoke this setup link, giving me:\ncurl -fsS -X DELETE 'http://127.0.0.1:4199/setup/OWzJfFkDkNiEp9vF-lL0mVacoPTV8-1k'\nMention that it expires 30 minutes after creation and I can paste this prompt into other agents until then.","expiresAt":"2026-10-18T23:08:28.577Z"}
